candidates.hypothesis:
Loop 3 cut a capped name's own ladder to cutToCeiling(capital, fullSize, cf). So a name that already sat at or below cf x fullSize was not cut at all. That happens when the name was cut and restored by its own ladder, or cut by the crowding check. So was a name the cap had only partly cut, i.e. one below full size when capped. Operator labels therefore weakened an agent's own ladder.

On research seeds 1-1600 there are 116 such cuts in 1002 shared-operator worlds. With loop 3's rule, 62 of them left the name more than 1% above what the same book without labels leaves it after the same cut, and the mean log(labelled/blind) was +0.229.

The fix: while a name is capped, the book keeps its "uncapped budget". That budget:
- starts at the budget the name held when the cap was set;
- is reallocated to its target without the cap, under the same band;
- is cut by the crowding check, run on the book with every capped name at its uncapped budget, and keeps that cut's ceiling until the name's book changes;
- is cut by its own ladder.
The ladder then cuts to cf x min(fullSize, uncapped).

This is exact against the blind book on scripted books. On arena seeds 1-1600: 7 cuts weaker than blind by >1% (max +9%), 19 harder by >1%, mean log -0.024, mean |log| 0.034.

No utility claim. Expected (and measured) neutral: about 3% of worlds are touched, and the change only ever cuts harder.
